---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.js';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Neyluno handles your data: files never leave your device, no account required, no invasive tracking."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="container prose-page">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
    <h1>Your files never leave your device</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This page explains — precisely, and in a way that is technically verifiable — how {site.name} handles
        your data. The short version: <strong>files are processed on your device, in your browser, and are
        never transmitted to any server.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>1. Your files</h2>
      <p>
        Every conversion, compression or generation runs in your browser using standard web technologies
        (Canvas, Web Crypto, pdf-lib, fflate, PDF.js). No file is uploaded: you can verify it yourself —
        open your browser's developer tools, watch the Network tab while using any tool, and you will see no
        request carrying your file.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What stays on your device — the complete list</h2>
      <p>
        A few conveniences are stored <em>locally</em>, never on our side. This table is exhaustive: if it is
        not listed here, Neyluno does not store it.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>What</th><th>Where</th><th>Key</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Theme preference (light / dark / system)</td><td>localStorage</td><td><code>qt-theme</code></td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Interface language (English / French)</td><td>localStorage</td><td><code>qt-lang</code></td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Recently used tools (max 8)</td><td>localStorage</td><td><code>qt-recents</code></td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Favorites</td><td>localStorage</td><td><code>qt-favorites</code></td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Saved workflows (max 20)</td><td>localStorage</td><td><code>qt-workflows</code></td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Handoff of your last processed file (one at a time)</td><td>IndexedDB</td><td><code>qt-handoff</code></td><td>10 minutes, then discarded</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        No tool remembers file names, contents or paths after you leave. You can erase everything at any
        time in <a href="/settings/">Settings → Clear all local data</a>, or by clearing this site's data
        in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>3. What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing by default. There is no account system and no analytics script loaded. If aggregated,
        non-identifying analytics are ever added, this page will say so first.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The site makes no call to advertising networks or tracking platforms. The hosting provider receives
        only ordinary web-server logs (IP address, requested page) as any static host does; those logs are
        not used to profile visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this page? Reach the maintainer at <strong>{site.contactEmail}</strong>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    padding-top: clamp(40px, 7vw, 72px);
    padding-bottom: 50px;
    max-width: 780px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.6vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 26px;
  }
</style>
